# A6L release: OPTIONAL module-ABI-CHANGING hardening (kernel-gaps 29 Sep 2026). NOT part of a6l-release.config.
# ARM64_SW_TTBR0_PAN emulates PAN on the ARMv8.0 Kryo 260 cores (no hardware PAN): user memory is unmapped while in the kernel.
# GKI enables it. It adds a field to thread_info, so the module CRCs change: every staged module (122 r5 + kernel-gaps) must be
# rebuilt against the resulting tree, and it costs a TTBR0 switch per uaccess. Decision for Pierre (docs/kernel-gaps-20260929.md).
CONFIG_ARM64_SW_TTBR0_PAN=y
